+---------------+---------+----------+-----------+---------+---------------------------+

How will we efficiently use the GPU resources?
Our LOBMAX implementation is built on MaxText (Google's JAX-based LLM framework) with the following optimizations:
- Flash Attention: O(S) memory complexity for sequence length S=12000, enabling batch size 22 per GPU
- Megablox Kernel: Sparse matrix multiplication for efficient MoE computation
- nn.scan: Efficient XLA compilation with gradient checkpointing (remat policy: save_dot_except_mlp)
- RoPE (llama3.1): Rotary position embedding with scaling for long sequences
- BFloat16: Mixed precision training for memory efficiency

Current achieved performance on GH200 (85GB HBM3):
- Dense 125M model: BSZ=22 per GPU, ~4.3% MFU, 13.9s/step
- Sequence length: 12000 tokens (24 tokens/message x 500 messages)
- Data parallelism: 4 GPUs per node

Expected MoE outcomes:
- 10x capacity scaling (30B effective model capacity with 3B computational cost)
- Regime specialization where different experts learn different market conditions
- Interpretable routing where expert activation patterns serve as market regime indicators
- Validated MoE infrastructure foundation for future expansion to larger scales

